{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/307738-cwod-newbie-looking-to-start-with-wraith","id":307738,"title":"CWoD Newbie: Looking to start with Wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-09T19:22:05-08:00","id":307738,"title":"CWoD Newbie: Looking to start with Wraith","content":"Hi CWoD Forums!<br /> <br /> I'm a NWoD fan myself, and I recently entered into a pact with a buddy of mine: I'd run a <i>Wraith: The Oblivion</i> game if he'd run a <i>Mummy: The Curse</i> game. He agreed, so now I've downloaded the 2e corebook to get started. That having been said, I'd like some advice from some real veterans on where I should go from the corebook to help me understand <i>Wraith</i> better. I've heard so many good things about the game, and want to be able to do it justice.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T20:11:30-08:00","id":307811,"title":"","content":"Read the whole thing, takes notes as relevant information is not always grouped well together.<br /> <br /> The Guildbooks have the best additional information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T07:39:39-08:00","id":308190,"title":"","content":"I highly recommend the Shadow Players Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T08:07:41-08:00","id":308220,"title":"","content":"It kind of depends what sort of Wraith game you want - it's a damn big game, and incomplete at that.<br /> <br /> Do you want to engage in a game of monster hunting as survival horror, where you're trying to pick off the monsters before they get you? Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> Do you want to get a better understanding of Stygian society, culture, and politics? The Guildbooks, Hierarchy, Book of Legions and Renegades.<br /> <br /> Want to better understand the Shadow? Shadow Players Guide.<br /> <br /> Want a look at wraithly cultures around the world? Wraith Players Guide, Shadow Players Guide, Dark Kingdom of Jade.<br /> <br /> Want to emulate The Crow? The Risen.<br /> <br /> Want a historical war story? Wraith: The Great War.<br /> <br /> Want to learn about those mortals who interact with the Restless Dead? Mediums: Speakers with the Dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T09:51:32-08:00","id":308308,"title":"","content":"I'd start with a skinlands/shadowlands-heavy storyarc. So the players can &quot;interact&quot; with thingsfamiliar to them while learning the basic rules.<br /> for the start read the core book 2nd ed. and get started. While the story moves on be sure to get familiar with the core book. Use the white wolf wikia to look up anything you don't understand and follow the links between topics as they interest you. If you find something you want to know more about find out wich book covers the topic.<br /> <br /> I highly recommend to use the wikia in the beginning. It lacks detail but it saves a lot of time. <br /> <br /> Think about it this way: you want to learn something new (wraithTheOblivion). The best way to learn things is to tackle them by the parts you find most interesting or most relevant for your needs. If you read a sourcebook and do not know if you are ever going to need it you surely will have a hard time on learning those &quot;useless&quot; things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:39:19-08:00","id":308348,"title":"","content":"Wr20 is also going to be the next KS, according to Deadguy Tweets, so there's also that if you just want to dive in and don't mind waiting a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T11:08:28-08:00","id":308376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/307738-cwod-newbie-looking-to-start-with-wraith?p=308348#post308348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wr20 is also going to be the next KS, according to Deadguy Tweets, so there's also that if you just want to dive in and don't mind waiting a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope for a wraith quick-start-guide stretch goal <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}